WEBVTT

00:00:17.530 --> 00:00:18.190
Do you have to do that here?

00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:22.230
Does it bother you, princess?

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:24.210
Trailer trash.

00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:26.150
Look, let's get something straight,

00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:27.410
you little Paris Hilton wannabe.

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:29.380
Maybe they put up with you at WaveSync,

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:29.980
but you...

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:31.060
You're on Reggie's turf now.

00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:33.850
She's not going to cut you any slack here or in the water.

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:36.210
If you don't like it, you can leave.

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:38.300
I'm not going anywhere.

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:39.740
Yeah? Well, neither is she.

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:41.110
Yo, anybody home?

00:00:42.530 --> 00:00:43.130
Hey, Bailey.

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:44.590
Wow.

00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:45.350
What are you doing here?

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:48.540
Um, I was over at WaveSync.

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:50.200
I guess your dad's lawyer's looking for you?

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:50.960
What, Morrison?

00:00:52.730 --> 00:00:54.150
Hey, guys, have I got any messages?

00:00:58.220 --> 00:00:58.680
Out of here.

00:00:59.270 --> 00:00:59.670
Let's go.

00:01:01.630 --> 00:01:14.100
That's disgusting care about proper protocol and what's the means my dad can hurt me one last time, okay?

00:01:15.010 --> 00:01:26.620
Yeah, I'll think about it. I have to go to Honolulu today before the reading of my father's will

00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:31.960
It's heavy.

00:01:32.140 --> 00:01:51.330
Hey, how's it looking?

00:01:54.580 --> 00:01:55.180
What's wrong?

00:01:57.340 --> 00:01:58.280
Been broke up with me.

00:01:59.540 --> 00:01:59.800
Sweet.

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:00.920
I'm so sorry.

00:02:01.410 --> 00:02:02.050
It's okay.

00:02:02.350 --> 00:02:03.070
It's my fault.

00:02:03.350 --> 00:02:06.760
I made a mess of my life.

00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:09.060
Now I'm not even gonna go on the tour.

00:02:10.720 --> 00:02:12.440
Is that why you tanked against Plankton?

00:02:12.790 --> 00:02:13.330
For Venn?

00:02:14.130 --> 00:02:15.150
Was it that obvious?

00:02:15.370 --> 00:02:18.090
I didn't wanna leave him.

00:02:19.770 --> 00:02:20.590
I gotta be blunt.

00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:22.080
That was stupid.

00:02:23.060 --> 00:02:25.060
You almost moved to Baltimore for Marcus.

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:26.600
But I didn't.

00:02:27.150 --> 00:02:29.790
Besides, Marcus is gonna be gone for four years minimum.

00:02:30.510 --> 00:02:33.760
You're talking like 12 weeks. That's nothing.

00:02:35.730 --> 00:02:44.900
I guess I thought that if I toured professionally, Finn would feel, I don't know, he thought he'd feel intimidated.

00:02:50.070 --> 00:02:56.490
Better than that guy.

00:02:56.770 --> 00:02:59.820
Are you kidding? You're better than every guy out there.

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:09.340
Uh, hi.

00:03:10.070 --> 00:03:10.930
Usun's that way.

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:12.260
I'm going to Honolulu.

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:14.920
I have to convince Dale I belong to him.

00:03:28.830 --> 00:03:29.270
Dale-y.

00:03:29.410 --> 00:03:29.970
It's your father.

00:03:30.620 --> 00:03:32.860
Oh, yeah, well, knowing him, he left me a nice note

00:03:32.860 --> 00:03:33.840
telling me to get my life together.

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:35.920
Yeah, well, what if he left you with something more than that?

00:03:36.060 --> 00:03:36.960
God, he won't!

00:03:39.710 --> 00:03:40.030
This!

00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:42.930
This is the last form of communication from your father.

00:03:43.090 --> 00:03:44.890
No matter what it says, I think you need to hear it.

00:03:44.990 --> 00:03:45.910
No, I don't!

00:03:46.520 --> 00:03:48.490
Come on, you can handle this.

00:03:49.740 --> 00:03:50.520
How do you know that?

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:52.450
You guys have seen you drop down a ten-foot wave

00:03:52.450 --> 00:03:53.670
without even batting an eyelash.

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:55.680
Well, a ten-foot wave can't forget my birthday.

00:03:57.440 --> 00:03:59.420
Well, I guess I better go throw something nice on.

00:04:01.020 --> 00:04:01.340
Why?

00:04:02.540 --> 00:04:03.800
Because I'm not letting you go through this alone.

00:04:07.310 --> 00:04:07.650
Thanks.

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:12.570
Yeah, I'll be back.

00:04:26.040 --> 00:04:29.200
Classic case of a guy not being able to handle being

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:29.980
with a strong .

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:34.420
successful woman. What are you guys talking about? Kai stunk on purpose

00:04:34.420 --> 00:04:43.120
yesterday because of Vin. Am I good? Yeah, have fun. Thank you. Vin doesn't seem like the type of

00:04:43.120 --> 00:04:54.780
guy to hold Kai back. He broke up with her. No way. Yeah. But they're like, you know, they're like

00:04:54.780 --> 00:04:59.230
the couple that are supposed to stay together forever. Yeah.

00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:11.930
Hey, you broke my fin oh yikes. Yeah, you did

00:05:30.440 --> 00:05:37.960
Hey, got your message.

00:05:38.220 --> 00:05:39.540
So you ran out of the house.

00:05:39.680 --> 00:05:40.400
I tried to catch up.

00:05:40.520 --> 00:05:41.580
What's going on?

00:05:42.860 --> 00:05:45.660
Well, you're still seeing your ex-wife.

00:05:46.770 --> 00:05:47.350
Oh, that.

00:05:47.740 --> 00:05:49.980
Yeah, um, it's not how it looked.

00:05:50.720 --> 00:05:52.240
Lacey and Ronnie have gotten kind of close,

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:53.500
and they asked me to sit down.

00:05:53.920 --> 00:05:55.140
I had no idea you were coming by.

00:05:55.650 --> 00:05:57.750
Well, then why did you text me to come over at 7?

00:05:58.750 --> 00:05:59.970
I told you to meet me at Rudeau.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:10.180
Ruby's at 8. My house at 7.

00:06:12.820 --> 00:06:13.220
Lacey.

00:06:13.950 --> 00:06:14.610
What about her?

00:06:14.890 --> 00:06:16.450
I think she must have texted you.

00:06:17.140 --> 00:06:18.120
Why would she do that?

00:06:18.700 --> 00:06:21.240
She gets a little protective and is probably just trying to scare you off.

00:06:24.100 --> 00:06:28.540
Well, Lacey's just gonna have to learn that I don't scare that easily.

00:06:31.110 --> 00:06:34.040
Justin, I'm falling in love with you.

00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:36.340
In love?

00:06:38.170 --> 00:06:39.750
Monica, we've only been hanging out a week.

00:06:40.480 --> 00:06:41.140
Don't worry.

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:43.100
I know that this is all moving a little fast,

00:06:43.300 --> 00:06:45.760
but I have a feeling that you and me,

00:06:46.890 --> 00:06:47.930
we're gonna make it.

00:06:48.660 --> 00:06:52.850
Uh, yeah, well...

00:07:00.640 --> 00:07:01.200
That was interesting.

00:07:01.610 --> 00:07:02.530
Couldn't have handled that.

00:07:03.780 --> 00:07:04.620
Thanks for coming.

00:07:06.330 --> 00:07:07.030
Oh, no worries.

00:07:08.970 --> 00:07:09.610
So how do you feel?

00:07:12.480 --> 00:07:13.760
I didn't think I could feel any worse.

00:07:15.560 --> 00:07:15.940
Wrong.

00:07:18.020 --> 00:07:18.880
Yeah, I know what you mean.

00:07:20.480 --> 00:07:20.760
You do?

00:07:21.460 --> 00:07:21.680
Yeah.

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:24.620
Despite everything, you were hoping for something.

00:07:25.370 --> 00:07:27.910
Some final gesture from your dad that would say...

00:07:27.910 --> 00:07:28.350
You loved me?

00:07:31.080 --> 00:07:34.350
I did. I just didn't know how to show it.

00:07:37.500 --> 00:07:38.460
I don't know what I'm going to do.

00:07:40.160 --> 00:07:42.460
But you can't stay here with the two evil stepsisters.

00:07:42.900 --> 00:07:43.580
That's for sure.

00:07:45.350 --> 00:07:47.670
All right, well, if you could wish for anything in the world right now, what would it be?

00:07:50.600 --> 00:07:51.900
For everything to be like it was.

00:07:53.000 --> 00:07:53.320
Meaning?

00:08:02.110 --> 00:08:03.430
I wish I could go back to Wavesync.

00:08:04.330 --> 00:08:17.570
Hey, hey.

00:08:17.800 --> 00:08:18.740
I need to talk to you.

00:08:21.800 --> 00:08:22.540
So, talk.

00:08:23.500 --> 00:08:26.190
Look, I see Kai every day, and when you were together,

00:08:26.470 --> 00:08:29.970
she was really happy, and now she won't admit it.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:38.220
But she's miserable about how it's worked out look she shouldn't be upset kai misses you I mean

00:08:38.220 --> 00:08:45.320
She's gonna surf the world make something of herself man. I'm just gonna be here. Do you want to be here?

00:08:45.460 --> 00:08:50.660
I wasn't giving gifts like her man. I know that kai's got more than a gift

00:08:51.740 --> 00:08:57.930
She's got guts. She puts herself out there. You think you're gonna just forget about a girl like that

00:09:02.580 --> 00:09:11.450
You're a little young to be writing off the rest of your life.

00:09:22.480 --> 00:09:25.980
Text me?

00:09:26.180 --> 00:09:26.760
Yeah, I did.

00:09:28.480 --> 00:09:29.840
Why would you want to ruin things with Monica?

00:09:30.540 --> 00:09:31.500
Okay, I can explain.

00:09:32.340 --> 00:09:33.340
She wasn't right for you.

00:09:33.500 --> 00:09:33.820
Really?

00:09:34.080 --> 00:09:35.640
I got a crappy vibe from her.

00:09:35.820 --> 00:09:36.900
A crappy vibe?

00:09:37.360 --> 00:09:38.380
Look, dude, don't get mad.

00:09:38.520 --> 00:09:39.460
I was just looking out for you.

00:09:39.620 --> 00:09:41.240
I don't need you looking out for me, Lacey.

00:09:41.550 --> 00:09:43.170
This is my life, not yours.

00:09:43.540 --> 00:09:45.760
If I want to date someone who has a crappy vibe,

00:09:46.040 --> 00:09:46.940
that's my call.

00:09:48.570 --> 00:09:48.930
Whatever.

00:09:50.130 --> 00:09:50.930
You're just like my mother.

00:09:52.310 --> 00:09:53.270
Is that what this is about?

00:09:56.280 --> 00:09:58.610
Lacey, I'm not going to disappear from your life

00:09:58.610 --> 00:09:59.690
just because I'm seeing someone.

00:10:01.760 --> 00:10:11.550
I will always be here, I promise, all right?

00:10:30.350 --> 00:10:32.010
to take me back, not after the way I've treated them.

00:10:33.100 --> 00:10:36.570
Lacey, Kai, especially Birdie.

00:10:37.060 --> 00:10:37.960
So cop to it.

00:10:38.610 --> 00:10:40.190
Say you're sorry and move on.

00:10:40.330 --> 00:10:41.990
You don't understand, I can't apologize.

00:10:42.470 --> 00:10:42.930
Why not?

00:10:43.360 --> 00:10:44.340
Because I don't know how.

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:45.360
What?

00:10:46.770 --> 00:10:47.910
My dad taught me two things.

00:10:48.820 --> 00:10:51.240
Never say you're sorry and never ask for help.

00:10:52.630 --> 00:10:53.370
So I never have.

00:10:54.520 --> 00:10:56.750
Well, there's a first time for everything.

00:10:58.420 --> 00:10:59.800
Listen, the key to a good apology.

00:11:00.160 --> 00:11:00.700
is demeaning.

00:11:10.710 --> 00:11:11.030
Luck.

00:11:16.520 --> 00:11:18.480
Obviously, Kai's conflicted about her surfing career.

00:11:18.800 --> 00:11:20.020
If she doesn't have the passion,

00:11:20.080 --> 00:11:21.940
I just don't know how convincing of an argument

00:11:21.940 --> 00:11:22.620
she can make to Dale.

00:11:30.540 --> 00:11:30.820
Yeah.

00:11:36.340 --> 00:11:40.210
Hi. Hello.

00:11:41.240 --> 00:11:41.580
Hang on.

00:11:42.260 --> 00:11:42.880
Do you want to come in?

00:11:43.390 --> 00:11:43.990
No, that's okay.

00:11:44.190 --> 00:11:46.450
I just needed to say something to you guys.

00:11:48.030 --> 00:11:49.830
Listen, I made a mistake.

00:11:50.030 --> 00:11:51.270
I didn't treat you guys right.

00:11:51.410 --> 00:11:57.280
I just wanted to say that I'm sorry.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:00.520
Is that it?

00:12:01.420 --> 00:12:05.100
I want to come back to WaveSync.

00:12:07.040 --> 00:12:07.940
Just like that?

00:12:08.370 --> 00:12:10.290
You think you can walk out on us in a snit

00:12:10.290 --> 00:12:13.040
and then come back when it suits you?

00:12:13.630 --> 00:12:18.010
Look, I won't blame you guys if I don't come back here, OK?

00:12:18.190 --> 00:12:19.550
Just let me know what you decide.

00:12:19.990 --> 00:12:29.900
Poor bonehead.

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:30.960
mistakes than I have.

00:12:32.160 --> 00:12:33.920
So, you want Dawn back in?

00:12:34.160 --> 00:12:35.160
What do you think, Justin?

00:12:36.200 --> 00:12:37.100
She's a great surfer.

00:12:37.500 --> 00:12:38.820
But you guys are the ones who gotta live with her.

00:12:39.450 --> 00:12:39.930
It's up to you.

00:12:40.780 --> 00:12:43.140
I can't turn my back on her when she's having a tough time.

00:12:43.560 --> 00:12:46.500
After how Dawn treated you, I tried to be her friend.

00:12:46.860 --> 00:12:47.740
We all tried.

00:12:48.290 --> 00:12:48.670
No.

00:12:49.120 --> 00:12:50.120
No, not like me.

00:12:50.490 --> 00:12:52.490
I opened up to her over and over again.

00:12:53.100 --> 00:12:55.280
If Dawn's capable of thinking about anyone but herself,

00:12:55.400 --> 00:12:56.320
she sure didn't show it.

00:12:56.780 --> 00:12:57.640
It's all about Dawn.

00:12:58.800 --> 00:12:59.020
Oh!

00:13:00.220 --> 00:13:00.860
What's going on here?

00:13:01.810 --> 00:13:03.910
Oh, little people versus Dawn Preston.

00:13:04.190 --> 00:13:04.570
Uh-oh.

00:13:05.030 --> 00:13:06.730
But, Bird, she said she was sorry.

00:13:07.100 --> 00:13:07.860
Come on!

00:13:08.130 --> 00:13:10.090
She said she's sorry because she's broke.

00:13:10.560 --> 00:13:14.720
She's stuck at plankton, in a bottom bunk, in a crappy house six blocks from the beach.

00:13:15.090 --> 00:13:17.650
She only wants back in because she misses all of this.

00:13:18.900 --> 00:13:19.940
Actually, you're wrong.

00:13:21.710 --> 00:13:23.310
About what, exactly?

00:13:23.770 --> 00:13:25.270
Dawn can afford to live anywhere she wants.

00:13:26.060 --> 00:13:27.080
She's got her inheritance.

00:13:27.730 --> 00:13:28.470
Twenty million dollars.

00:13:30.700 --> 00:13:31.020
What?

00:13:31.600 --> 00:13:31.960
Whoa.

00:13:34.830 --> 00:13:35.190
OK.

00:13:35.830 --> 00:13:37.590
That doesn't make any sense.

00:13:39.250 --> 00:13:41.050
Why would she want to move back in with us?

00:13:56.680 --> 00:13:57.120
So good.

00:14:09.470 --> 00:14:13.520
Hey, Monica, what are you doing here?

00:14:14.100 --> 00:14:16.900
Well, I was very surprised when I got a call from this one.

00:14:17.810 --> 00:14:18.550
You called her?

00:14:18.730 --> 00:14:21.540
Yeah, I wanted to apologize for the stunt I pulled yesterday.

00:14:21.920 --> 00:14:22.680
We cleared the air.

00:14:23.150 --> 00:14:23.610
Oh, good.

00:14:23.920 --> 00:14:25.500
No, I made senti. I'll be right back.

00:14:25.600 --> 00:14:26.240
Oh, okay, good.

00:14:27.920 --> 00:14:28.140
Doing?

00:14:28.440 --> 00:14:29.680
I'm just trying to make things right.

00:14:30.190 --> 00:14:30.990
This isn't right.

00:14:31.210 --> 00:14:32.620
I thought you liked her.

00:14:33.120 --> 00:14:34.040
I never said that.

00:14:34.260 --> 00:14:37.340
I mean, she's okay, but now's not the time to encourage her.

00:14:37.570 --> 00:14:39.560
So, enjoy your shuffleboard.

00:14:40.420 --> 00:14:41.760
Justin, I hate shuffleboard.

00:14:43.060 --> 00:14:43.940
Oh, awesome.

00:14:46.220 --> 00:14:46.940
Oh, it's good.

00:14:47.120 --> 00:14:47.620
But you know what?

00:14:47.680 --> 00:14:49.120
Unfortunately, I have to drive into Waikiki.

00:14:49.280 --> 00:14:53.310
I got a busy day, which means you guys get to spend the entire day together.

00:14:54.420 --> 00:14:54.740
See ya.

00:14:54.880 --> 00:14:58.600
Can I go to a movie?

00:15:00.350 --> 00:15:16.310
Here to give me the bad news?

00:15:17.210 --> 00:15:18.420
No, I'm not.

00:15:20.020 --> 00:15:20.620
You're back in.

00:15:22.500 --> 00:15:24.420
You know, you're lucky Kai and Lacey are so forgiving.

00:15:24.670 --> 00:15:27.950
I voted no, but you got your way, as usual.

00:15:28.560 --> 00:15:28.940
Happy?

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:33.100
No, but I'm grateful.

00:15:34.390 --> 00:15:35.170
No, I don't get it.

00:15:35.450 --> 00:15:36.670
Bailey told us that you got your money,

00:15:36.690 --> 00:15:38.630
so why is it so important for you to come back here?

00:15:40.620 --> 00:15:42.080
Came back because it's the only place

00:15:42.080 --> 00:15:43.100
it's ever felt like home.

00:15:44.780 --> 00:15:48.500
Came back because it's the only place

00:15:48.500 --> 00:15:49.500
where I felt like I had a family.

00:15:53.200 --> 00:15:54.560
I guess I had to leave to realize that.

00:16:01.200 --> 00:16:02.660
Because I don't really know you, Dawn.

00:16:02.860 --> 00:16:03.620
I never did.

00:16:03.800 --> 00:16:04.920
How can you say that?

00:16:05.750 --> 00:16:08.300
We shared a room together and clothes.

00:16:09.320 --> 00:16:10.300
We shared feelings.

00:16:10.380 --> 00:16:11.430
No, no.

00:16:11.960 --> 00:16:13.600
I shared my feelings.

00:16:13.760 --> 00:16:14.600
You never did.

00:16:15.250 --> 00:16:17.270
The only thing I know about you is that you're rich,

00:16:17.310 --> 00:16:19.010
and the only person you think about is yourself.

00:16:20.370 --> 00:16:22.690
Oh, and that you don't look good in yellow.

00:16:23.120 --> 00:16:23.920
But that's about it.

00:16:25.170 --> 00:16:26.910
We never talked about anything that mattered.

00:16:31.850 --> 00:16:35.200
It was when I was eight years old, the last time I cried.

00:16:35.440 --> 00:16:44.120
I was at my brother's funeral, and my dad told me to stop embarrassing him.

00:16:46.330 --> 00:16:47.050
You had a brother?

00:16:49.460 --> 00:16:50.900
What happened?

00:16:51.200 --> 00:16:52.690
A big accident.

00:16:53.470 --> 00:16:55.010
He just got his driver's license.

00:17:01.240 --> 00:17:03.300
Don, I'm so sorry.

00:17:04.020 --> 00:17:07.480
Yeah, that's what I kept telling my dad.

00:17:07.680 --> 00:17:10.520
I'm sorry.

00:17:10.720 --> 00:17:13.900
I just felt so guilty, you know?

00:17:15.280 --> 00:17:16.340
It wasn't your fault.

00:17:16.440 --> 00:17:17.260
Why'd you feel guilty?

00:17:17.480 --> 00:17:29.960
The way he'd look at me, like...

00:17:31.500 --> 00:17:32.720
Like the wrong child died.

00:17:32.900 --> 00:17:46.120
And after that, I just kind of learned to boil everything up to the side.

00:17:46.220 --> 00:17:49.350
And I didn't, never let it out again, you know?

00:17:51.690 --> 00:17:52.790
It's okay to cry.

00:17:52.990 --> 00:17:58.620
You told me that.

00:18:03.580 --> 00:18:05.920
Now you know something besides the fact that I look bad in yellow.

00:18:06.360 --> 00:18:20.070
Full summer.

00:18:20.960 --> 00:18:21.340
I know.

00:18:24.230 --> 00:18:25.570
I'm going to miss everyone so much.

00:18:26.240 --> 00:18:27.220
Did you say goodbye to Vin?

00:18:29.390 --> 00:18:29.690
No.

00:18:30.160 --> 00:18:30.540
We're done.

00:18:31.280 --> 00:18:31.640
Really?

00:18:32.940 --> 00:18:33.260
Yeah.

00:18:36.270 --> 00:18:37.290
Who get you those towels?

00:18:49.920 --> 00:18:50.640
He wasn't a bad guy.

00:18:51.160 --> 00:18:52.140
He had a sense of humor.

00:18:52.340 --> 00:18:54.140
He was tough and independent,

00:18:54.180 --> 00:18:56.360
and I guess I got that from him.

00:18:56.880 --> 00:18:57.480
That's nice.

00:18:58.390 --> 00:18:59.150
So how do you feel now?

00:19:00.830 --> 00:19:02.550
A little shaky, a little embarrassed,

00:19:02.710 --> 00:19:05.410
but I'm also just really excited to be back here.

00:19:06.080 --> 00:19:07.240
Cool, I'm excited too.

00:19:07.420 --> 00:19:07.760
Yeah.

00:19:11.280 --> 00:19:15.020
Hey, come back.

00:19:16.140 --> 00:19:27.260
Hi, what are you doing here?

00:19:30.250 --> 00:19:32.090
I couldn't leave tomorrow with things the way they are.

00:19:34.080 --> 00:19:35.560
Yeah, I was just on my way to see you.

00:19:35.740 --> 00:19:36.880
I just had to pick something up.

00:19:38.570 --> 00:19:39.390
Where's your sculptures?

00:19:40.620 --> 00:19:41.260
At the studio.

00:19:42.480 --> 00:19:43.060
What studio?

00:19:43.850 --> 00:19:44.450
At the college.

00:19:44.830 --> 00:19:47.740
I signed up for an art course.

00:19:48.200 --> 00:19:48.700
You did?

00:19:49.500 --> 00:19:49.860
Yep.

00:19:51.100 --> 00:19:56.410
And I figured, if you believe in me, maybe I should believe in myself.

00:19:59.220 --> 00:19:59.980
I want you to go all the way.

00:20:00.480 --> 00:20:03.080
And I'm gonna do my best to keep up with you.

00:20:03.260 --> 00:20:04.220
I don't care if you don't.

00:20:05.560 --> 00:20:05.940
I know.

00:20:12.300 --> 00:20:14.800
Travel the world all the summer, and I'm not.

00:20:16.990 --> 00:20:18.840
So, I made you this.

00:20:22.890 --> 00:20:23.150
Come on.

00:20:26.260 --> 00:20:27.700
Take a piece of me every place you go.

00:20:31.280 --> 00:20:44.800
My grind is a super shallow right, so if you're going down, fall flat.

00:20:52.020 --> 00:20:53.340
Hi, what's going on?

00:20:54.270 --> 00:20:55.570
Kai, you're right here.

00:20:56.700 --> 00:20:57.760
I'm not ready to go yet.

00:20:58.340 --> 00:20:58.780
Why not?

00:21:00.440 --> 00:21:01.300
So I want to make a toast.

00:21:01.530 --> 00:21:02.050
Two.

00:21:03.220 --> 00:21:03.680
Two.

00:21:04.600 --> 00:21:05.920
One last paddle out.

00:21:06.800 --> 00:21:07.060
Yeah!

00:21:33.320 --> 00:21:44.040
Time to try
